WEBVTT

00:00:10.300 --> 00:00:11.920
<i>Otome</i>:

00:00:11.920 --> 00:00:14.840
A maiden, sweet-smelling as a flower,

00:00:14.840 --> 00:00:20.140
a single bud blooming in a tranquil
garden, pure and dignified.

00:00:20.140 --> 00:00:24.230
Too shy to even speak of love or romance,

00:00:24.230 --> 00:00:27.440
she dares not allow herself
to dream of a kiss.

00:00:28.690 --> 00:00:34.320
Even so, she is now becoming
a butterfly, drawing closer to sip

00:00:34.320 --> 00:00:36.610
the forbidden nectar of love.

00:00:44.790 --> 00:00:52.590
"Taisho Otome Fairy Tale"

00:01:56.950 --> 00:02:02.080
"Taisho Otome Fairy Tale"

00:02:03.200 --> 00:02:07.000
"Episode 8"
"Tamahiko Goes to School"

00:02:09.460 --> 00:02:11.750
"Dear Father,

00:02:11.750 --> 00:02:16.590
Though I am spending my days as
though I were dead, as you directed,

00:02:16.590 --> 00:02:18.720
I would like to attend school."

00:02:22.680 --> 00:02:24.760
This is the fifth letter I've sent.

00:02:26.020 --> 00:02:28.730
I've heard nothing back from Father.

00:02:30.560 --> 00:02:33.110
Shima-<i>san</i>! The mail's here!

00:02:33.110 --> 00:02:34.650
Coming!

00:02:34.650 --> 00:02:36.320
Thank you very much.

00:02:39.320 --> 00:02:40.410
Is it from Father?

00:02:44.120 --> 00:02:45.910
Ah, from Midori-<i>san</i>.

00:02:45.910 --> 00:02:48.660
But there's another letter from Kobe.

00:02:48.660 --> 00:02:52.880
Oh. I know you and Tamako
were corresponding.

00:02:52.880 --> 00:02:55.250
No--this is addressed to you.

00:02:55.250 --> 00:02:56.250
Huh?

00:02:58.210 --> 00:03:01.630
It's from Uncle Tamasuke.
Whatever could it be?

00:03:04.470 --> 00:03:10.350
"Tamahiko: Tamako frequently keeps
me apprised of your situation.

00:03:10.350 --> 00:03:13.190
She has taken to her
studies with enthusiasm,

00:03:13.190 --> 00:03:17.360
her desire to become a doctor
now stronger than ever.

00:03:17.360 --> 00:03:22.320
By the way, Tamahiko... I wonder if
you won't let me assist <i>you </i>as well."

00:03:22.320 --> 00:03:23.320
What?!

00:03:24.910 --> 00:03:29.660
Oh, my! My brother says he's studying
so he can go back to school!

00:03:30.750 --> 00:03:32.290
Tamahiko is?

00:03:32.290 --> 00:03:36.670
Yes: the same Tamahiko who can't
do anything of his own volition--

00:03:36.670 --> 00:03:39.340
and who can barely move.

00:03:39.340 --> 00:03:42.590
For him, that's a lot of determination!

00:03:42.590 --> 00:03:45.100
All thanks to Yuzu, I'm sure.

00:03:47.260 --> 00:03:48.720
Still...

00:03:48.720 --> 00:03:52.310
Will Father even allow it?

00:03:52.310 --> 00:03:53.650
That's worrying.

00:03:56.190 --> 00:03:57.440
I see...

00:03:59.820 --> 00:04:03.570
"It would be a terrible waste for
an excellent young man like you

00:04:03.570 --> 00:04:05.530
not to return to school.

00:04:05.530 --> 00:04:08.410
I hereby offer my support, and gladly.

00:04:08.410 --> 00:04:11.870
I understand you may be overwhelmed
by this sudden proposal,

00:04:11.870 --> 00:04:14.170
but please consider it
in a positive light."

00:04:16.960 --> 00:04:19.880
Hello? This is Tamahiko.

00:04:19.880 --> 00:04:21.300
Yes.

00:04:21.300 --> 00:04:24.260
Um... I read your letter.

00:04:25.510 --> 00:04:27.930
And... yes. Please.

00:04:29.930 --> 00:04:30.930
Yes.

00:04:31.980 --> 00:04:34.190
Yes... yes.

00:04:34.190 --> 00:04:38.230
I'll repay this kindness
one day, I swear it.

00:04:38.230 --> 00:04:40.030
Thank you so much.

00:04:41.940 --> 00:04:46.610
I would aim to skip a grade and transfer
into the second year of high school.

00:04:47.780 --> 00:04:50.200
I feel like no amount of
studying will be enough.

00:04:52.750 --> 00:04:56.170
But it's only natural
that I'd do all this.

00:04:56.170 --> 00:04:59.380
Anything to regain the time
I'd lost as a shut-in.

00:04:59.380 --> 00:05:00.710
And...

00:05:00.710 --> 00:05:03.050
...to become someone
who can keep Yuzu safe.

00:05:06.760 --> 00:05:09.760
Tamahiko! Working hard?

00:05:09.760 --> 00:05:12.470
Ryo-<i>san</i>! What are you doing here?

00:05:12.470 --> 00:05:14.770
Just checking on our scholar!

00:05:14.770 --> 00:05:18.310
I want to be in Tamahiko's corner, too.

00:05:18.310 --> 00:05:19.770
I'll just be borrowing your kitchen!

00:05:19.770 --> 00:05:20.770
Hey!

00:05:21.570 --> 00:05:25.280
Tamahiko-<i>sama </i>doesn't
need any more tending to!

00:05:25.280 --> 00:05:27.450
Honestly, that Ryo-<i>san</i>...

00:05:29.870 --> 00:05:32.240
Oh, Yuzu, don't be so polite!

00:05:32.240 --> 00:05:34.040
This isn't about politeness!

00:05:34.040 --> 00:05:35.500
I can't concentrate...

00:05:37.290 --> 00:05:38.630
Then, one day...

00:05:38.630 --> 00:05:41.170
This is <i>big</i>! <i>Really </i>big!

00:05:42.090 --> 00:05:44.210
Is... is this...

00:05:44.210 --> 00:05:45.880
Amazing, right?

00:05:46.880 --> 00:05:48.390
What's going on?

00:05:48.390 --> 00:05:49.930
Tamahiko-<i>sama</i>!

00:05:49.930 --> 00:05:54.350
It looks like Kotori Shiratori will
be coming to Chiba Station!

00:05:54.350 --> 00:05:55.350
Huh!

00:05:56.270 --> 00:05:58.730
Why don't we all go?

00:05:58.730 --> 00:06:01.770
But you have your studies...

00:06:07.900 --> 00:06:10.700
Come with us, Tamahiko-<i>sensei</i>!

00:06:10.700 --> 00:06:11.530
Huh?

00:06:11.530 --> 00:06:13.410
Come with us!

00:06:13.410 --> 00:06:15.580
You need a breather now and then.

00:06:15.580 --> 00:06:19.460
Miss Yuzu, you'd be happier
if he came along, right?

00:06:22.630 --> 00:06:25.260
Well, it <i>is </i>a real opportunity...

00:06:25.260 --> 00:06:27.010
Hooray!

00:06:29.430 --> 00:06:31.470
"Chiba Station"

00:06:31.720 --> 00:06:33.850
Over here, Tamahiko-<i>sama</i>!

00:06:33.850 --> 00:06:35.350
Hurry up!

00:06:35.350 --> 00:06:37.020
She's about to start!

00:06:37.020 --> 00:06:38.270
Yes, coming...

00:06:39.940 --> 00:06:41.520
It's the real deal!

00:06:41.520 --> 00:06:44.230
She's way cuter than her photographs!

00:06:55.990 --> 00:07:02.630
♬ The bird doesn't fly,
but cries and cries ♬

00:07:02.630 --> 00:07:08.720
♬ It's always crying, all alone ♬

00:07:08.720 --> 00:07:15.600
♬ In the shadow of a tree,
with the moon gazing down ♬

00:07:15.600 --> 00:07:21.560
♬ He sheds a tear:
"It's so lonely, all alone" ♬

00:07:21.560 --> 00:07:28.570
♬ "You're not alone,"
replies the spring breeze ♬

00:07:28.570 --> 00:07:34.990
♬ Do re mi fa so gently it blows ♬

00:07:34.990 --> 00:07:41.460
♬ So la ti do: the bird
flutters into the sky ♬

00:07:53.220 --> 00:07:56.100
Hello! I'm Kotori Shiratori.

00:07:56.100 --> 00:07:59.100
There's so many of you
here to see me today--

00:07:59.100 --> 00:08:01.390
I'm so very grateful to you all!

00:08:01.390 --> 00:08:03.400
Kotori-<i>chan</i>!

00:08:09.780 --> 00:08:11.740
Next up is one of my favorites.

00:08:12.900 --> 00:08:15.530
It's a song from the
far-off country of Ireland.

00:08:22.120 --> 00:08:28.250
♬ Believe me, if all those
endearing young charms ♬

00:08:28.250 --> 00:08:30.130
What is this? Another language?

00:08:30.130 --> 00:08:32.920
But it's such a wonderful, gentle tune.

00:08:35.510 --> 00:08:36.510
Sensei?

00:08:38.010 --> 00:08:40.430
What's she saying?

00:08:40.430 --> 00:08:41.600
Well...

00:08:44.190 --> 00:08:46.440
"Please trust in me.

00:08:47.770 --> 00:08:52.940
I'll keep on loving you forever."

00:08:54.490 --> 00:08:55.490
Yuzu?

00:08:56.700 --> 00:08:59.330
It's good that we came.

00:09:01.790 --> 00:09:02.790
Yes.

00:09:04.080 --> 00:09:09.500
♬ Would entwine itself verdantly still ♬

00:09:16.090 --> 00:09:18.680
"Transfer Examination"

00:09:40.200 --> 00:09:42.490
This is it: time for school.

00:09:42.490 --> 00:09:45.830
Somehow <i>I'm </i>the nervous one.

00:09:46.750 --> 00:09:50.340
Here's your lunch.
I'll put it in your bag.

00:09:50.340 --> 00:09:51.340
Thanks.

00:09:53.210 --> 00:09:56.630
Oh... maybe I'll go with you partway...

00:09:56.630 --> 00:09:58.300
You worry too much.

00:09:59.680 --> 00:10:02.510
I'm a shut-in and a pessimist.

00:10:03.770 --> 00:10:05.730
I lost my mother

00:10:05.730 --> 00:10:08.350
and the use of my right hand.

00:10:08.350 --> 00:10:10.060
Forsaken by my father...

00:10:14.030 --> 00:10:16.150
"I'm cursed--stay away"

00:10:14.030 --> 00:10:16.150
...with no friends to stand by me.

00:10:17.610 --> 00:10:19.860
I've been living as though I were dead.

00:10:22.620 --> 00:10:24.740
But I have to change.

00:10:26.660 --> 00:10:28.580
I'll be fine, Yuzu.

00:10:28.580 --> 00:10:30.460
See you later.

00:10:30.460 --> 00:10:32.090
Yes--see you later!

00:10:33.340 --> 00:10:35.420
I'm taking that first step at last.

00:10:38.680 --> 00:10:41.340
"Katsuragi High School"

00:10:38.680 --> 00:10:41.340
--Morning.
--Good morning.

00:10:42.100 --> 00:10:43.260
<i>There's </i>a big 'un!

00:10:43.260 --> 00:10:45.100
--So tall!
--That height...

00:10:45.520 --> 00:10:47.770
"Staff Room"
"buzz buzz"

00:10:50.440 --> 00:10:51.810
Wow!

00:10:51.810 --> 00:10:54.900
No way would someone like <i>him</i>
come to our school!

00:10:55.400 --> 00:11:00.610
E-Excuse me! Um... today's my first...

00:11:00.610 --> 00:11:04.450
Ah, you'd be our second transfer student.

00:11:04.450 --> 00:11:05.740
Second?

00:11:09.540 --> 00:11:12.000
"Year 2, Class B Science"

00:11:13.130 --> 00:11:17.340
Hakaru Shiratori. I'm here from
the Third Higher School.

00:11:17.340 --> 00:11:18.970
Shi--Shiratori?

00:11:18.970 --> 00:11:21.430
So you're Kotori Shiratori's--

00:11:21.430 --> 00:11:23.470
Yes: her twin brother.

00:11:25.970 --> 00:11:30.640
Kotori-<i>chan </i>and I have moved
in with relatives in Chiba.

00:11:30.640 --> 00:11:32.810
Here's to a great year!

00:11:32.810 --> 00:11:34.440
Whoa! He looks just like her!

00:11:34.440 --> 00:11:37.190
I wanna meet Kotori-<i>chan</i>!

00:11:37.190 --> 00:11:38.990
Next up: Shima-<i>kun</i>.

00:11:40.150 --> 00:11:41.650
Oh, right.

00:11:41.650 --> 00:11:44.950
I'm, uh... Tamahiko... Shima.

00:11:46.660 --> 00:11:50.460
Shima? As in the diabolical Shima family?

00:11:50.460 --> 00:11:52.870
No, it can't be.

00:11:52.870 --> 00:11:58.800
Now, Shima-<i>kun </i>lost the use of
his right hand in an accident.

00:11:58.800 --> 00:12:02.050
Go easy on him, all right?

00:12:02.050 --> 00:12:05.050
Probably best not to get involved at all.

00:12:09.180 --> 00:12:12.190
Shiratori-<i>kun</i>, join us at the café later?

00:12:12.190 --> 00:12:14.230
How about joining the baseball club?

00:12:14.230 --> 00:12:17.820
If there's anything you
don't understand, just ask!

00:12:17.820 --> 00:12:19.280
By the way, is Kotori-<i>cha</i>--

00:12:19.280 --> 00:12:23.200
Hey! Gym class is next!
Hurry up and change!

00:12:23.200 --> 00:12:24.280
Damn!

00:12:25.530 --> 00:12:26.660
C'mon!

00:12:33.620 --> 00:12:34.960
Too slow!

00:12:34.960 --> 00:12:36.210
Sorry...

00:12:38.460 --> 00:12:42.340
Everyone run the yard for the rest of
the hour! That's joint responsibility!

00:12:44.380 --> 00:12:48.010
Man, this is harsh. Why us?

00:12:48.010 --> 00:12:51.640
I mean, if you're that slow,
just ask for help.

00:12:57.480 --> 00:12:59.940
Yes! Lunchtime at last!

00:13:00.820 --> 00:13:02.900
Wanna come to the dorms, Shiratori-<i>kun</i>?

00:13:02.900 --> 00:13:04.860
We can eat together.

00:13:04.860 --> 00:13:08.450
And you can tell us about Kotori-<i>chan</i>!

00:13:08.450 --> 00:13:09.450
I...

00:13:12.620 --> 00:13:14.330
C'mon, let's go!

00:13:24.840 --> 00:13:26.090
Let's see.

00:13:27.340 --> 00:13:30.510
Ooh! Yuzu really put her
best foot forward.

00:13:34.980 --> 00:13:36.940
Mmm... so good.

00:13:36.940 --> 00:13:39.610
Tasty in a different way,
as a boxed lunch.

00:13:47.240 --> 00:13:48.570
So good...

00:13:50.530 --> 00:13:51.790
...so good...

00:14:07.720 --> 00:14:11.350
You must be wondering
about Tamahiko-<i>sama</i>, too.

00:14:15.930 --> 00:14:18.520
Ah, Tamahiko-<i>sama</i>...

00:14:18.520 --> 00:14:21.230
I hope he's not feeling uncomfortable.

00:14:21.650 --> 00:14:24.190
I wonder if he's made friends?

00:14:26.490 --> 00:14:30.030
Today you'll be drawing
someone important to you.

00:14:30.030 --> 00:14:32.990
"Picture it in your mind, put it on paper"

00:14:30.030 --> 00:14:32.990
A family member, that
special someone--anyone will do!

00:14:33.490 --> 00:14:35.120
My mom.

00:14:35.120 --> 00:14:37.250
Miyo-<i>chan</i>, the maid at the café!

00:14:40.420 --> 00:14:42.710
Can I move next to you?

00:14:42.710 --> 00:14:43.710
Huh?

00:14:48.720 --> 00:14:50.340
Well? How goes it?

00:14:50.590 --> 00:14:52.600
"Me" "Yuzuki making my lunch"

00:14:59.390 --> 00:15:00.770
You're good!

00:15:01.350 --> 00:15:04.520
Look. Weren't you just
holding back laughter?

00:15:04.520 --> 00:15:06.740
Why, I would <i>never </i>laugh!

00:15:14.030 --> 00:15:19.790
No one asked you to sign this...
<i>delightful </i>portrait, and yet here we are!

00:15:19.790 --> 00:15:21.250
What a masterpiece!

00:15:23.670 --> 00:15:25.550
Your true feelings are showing.

00:15:27.670 --> 00:15:29.380
Okay, you got me.

00:15:31.630 --> 00:15:34.260
Your portrait is the pits.

00:15:35.600 --> 00:15:38.390
Here, use mine for reference.

00:15:38.390 --> 00:15:40.480
Now <i>this </i>is a pro-level portrait.

00:15:44.480 --> 00:15:45.770
Who's that?

00:15:45.770 --> 00:15:49.030
I-It's Kotori-<i>chan</i>--obviously!

00:15:49.030 --> 00:15:54.320
If that's what she looks like to you,
you need better glasses--<i>now</i>.

00:15:54.320 --> 00:15:56.410
Oh, yeah? Says you!

00:15:56.410 --> 00:15:58.910
No, I mean it.

00:15:58.910 --> 00:16:00.710
Your portrait is worse!

00:16:00.710 --> 00:16:03.670
--No, yours is worse.
--No, <i>yours </i>is worse!

00:16:03.670 --> 00:16:06.040
No, <i>yours </i>is worse.

00:16:06.040 --> 00:16:08.670
Hey, pipe down over there!

00:16:08.670 --> 00:16:10.840
Yikes! What <i>are </i>these?!

00:16:10.840 --> 00:16:13.590
No slapdash work!
I want serious effort here!

00:16:13.590 --> 00:16:15.260
Art is an important subject!

00:16:15.260 --> 00:16:17.720
--Just because you're
brand-new doesn't mean...
--What was that all about?

00:16:18.350 --> 00:16:19.640
I'm home!

00:16:19.640 --> 00:16:20.680
Coming!

00:16:25.310 --> 00:16:27.150
Welcome home,

00:16:27.150 --> 00:16:28.570
Tamahiko-<i>sama</i>!

00:16:31.900 --> 00:16:33.360
Hello there!

00:16:34.320 --> 00:16:37.740
Yuzu, this is Hakaru Shiratori,
from my class.

00:16:37.740 --> 00:16:38.660
He's Shiratori Koto--

00:16:38.660 --> 00:16:41.160
Oh, my! Welcome!

00:16:41.160 --> 00:16:44.290
Please, come in!
I'll bring some tea right away!

00:16:45.420 --> 00:16:48.460
--What's got <i>her </i>so excited?
--Have a seat!

00:16:48.460 --> 00:16:52.260
Probably thrilled to see such
a handsome young man as myself.

00:16:54.340 --> 00:16:57.800
Ah, your homework is to draw each other?

00:16:57.800 --> 00:16:59.180
So you came here.

00:16:59.180 --> 00:17:02.020
Sorry to pop by so suddenly!

00:17:02.020 --> 00:17:05.020
Not at all. Sounds like a fun assignment.

00:17:05.020 --> 00:17:08.060
Less assignment, more punishment.

00:17:08.060 --> 00:17:10.530
Good luck, you two!

00:17:15.950 --> 00:17:17.570
Hey, Shima-<i>kun</i>...

00:17:17.570 --> 00:17:18.870
What?

00:17:18.870 --> 00:17:21.370
Yuzu-<i>chan</i>'s one nice girl.

00:17:21.370 --> 00:17:22.370
Mmm.

00:17:23.160 --> 00:17:26.250
And such an adorable smile!

00:17:26.250 --> 00:17:27.750
Yeah.

00:17:27.750 --> 00:17:30.550
I like that smile of hers, too.

00:17:30.550 --> 00:17:32.960
It just makes me so happy.

00:17:39.300 --> 00:17:42.390
I, uh... I'll go get more tea.

00:17:42.390 --> 00:17:44.430
Thanks!

00:17:44.430 --> 00:17:45.350
Yuzu?

00:17:45.350 --> 00:17:46.810
Yes?

00:17:46.810 --> 00:17:49.560
Could we get more tea?

00:17:49.560 --> 00:17:50.690
Oh, sure.

00:17:51.780 --> 00:17:53.230
Tamahiko-<i>sama</i>?

00:17:53.230 --> 00:17:55.280
How was school?

00:17:57.860 --> 00:17:59.780
Well...

00:17:59.780 --> 00:18:02.910
There's nothing like a new school.

00:18:02.910 --> 00:18:05.460
The teaching materials are extensive.

00:18:05.460 --> 00:18:07.500
The teachers are outstanding.

00:18:07.500 --> 00:18:12.000
The students are all generous
and good-natured, too.

00:18:12.000 --> 00:18:14.630
We ran a marathon in gym class today.

00:18:14.630 --> 00:18:18.180
There we were, running and
griping about how hard it was.

00:18:18.180 --> 00:18:21.600
But I ate your lunch afterward,
Yuzu, and it was really special.

00:18:26.520 --> 00:18:31.520
I'm sorry. I've just been
so anxious all day.

00:18:32.480 --> 00:18:34.280
I see now.

00:18:34.280 --> 00:18:37.280
You've made a friend
in Shiratori-<i>san </i>here,

00:18:37.280 --> 00:18:40.450
even bringing him home with you.

00:18:40.450 --> 00:18:41.620
Uh-huh.

00:18:41.620 --> 00:18:43.660
I'm sorry, Yuzu.

00:18:45.580 --> 00:18:50.000
All right--I'll do my best at making
the rest of your lunches, too!

00:18:50.000 --> 00:18:51.250
Thanks, Yuzu.

00:18:52.380 --> 00:18:53.920
That liar.

00:18:55.260 --> 00:18:56.670
--It's done!
--It's done!

00:18:58.170 --> 00:19:00.760
"Shima-<i>kun</i>" "Shiratori-<i>kun</i>"

00:18:58.170 --> 00:19:00.760
Oho... so this is me.

00:19:00.760 --> 00:19:04.350
What, are you going to say
it's the pits again?

00:19:04.350 --> 00:19:07.980
Nuh-uh. Upon closer inspection,
I really quite like it.

00:19:07.980 --> 00:19:09.980
What? Why?

00:19:09.980 --> 00:19:13.650
You really have a way with
your subjects' smiling faces.

00:19:13.650 --> 00:19:15.940
Same thing with Yuzu-<i>chan</i>'s portrait.

00:19:17.570 --> 00:19:21.450
Yuzu's smile is like the spring.

00:19:21.450 --> 00:19:24.200
Yes: it <i>is </i>the very spring itself.

00:19:25.370 --> 00:19:26.870
Still...

00:19:26.870 --> 00:19:30.290
It's not right to make her
smile with a lie, now, is it?

00:19:31.330 --> 00:19:33.250
You heard that?

00:19:33.250 --> 00:19:34.460
Sorry.

00:19:35.710 --> 00:19:41.050
I just... I didn't want
to make her unhappy.

00:19:41.050 --> 00:19:44.890
I want to make her smile...
even if I had to lie.

00:19:46.180 --> 00:19:50.100
I should be honest with her.

00:19:50.100 --> 00:19:51.850
Dummy.

00:19:51.850 --> 00:19:54.770
Just turn your lies into the truth.

00:19:54.770 --> 00:19:58.280
Then you won't have lied at all.

00:19:58.280 --> 00:20:02.820
Lies are bad news, but I do think
you lied for a good reason.

00:20:02.820 --> 00:20:04.240
Shiratori-<i>kun</i>...

00:20:05.280 --> 00:20:06.990
I mean...

00:20:06.990 --> 00:20:09.330
That's pretty rich coming from me.

00:20:11.120 --> 00:20:13.210
Nothing!

00:20:13.210 --> 00:20:15.290
Dinner's ready!

00:20:15.290 --> 00:20:17.250
Great! Thanks!

00:20:18.710 --> 00:20:21.760
Turn my lies into the truth, huh?

00:20:26.510 --> 00:20:30.020
Oh, wow! What is this? It's delicious!

00:20:30.020 --> 00:20:32.270
It's called <i>hittsumi</i>.

00:20:32.270 --> 00:20:36.360
Huh! You'll make a fine wife, Yuzu-<i>chan</i>.

00:20:36.360 --> 00:20:38.230
Thank you very much!

00:20:38.230 --> 00:20:41.400
Now <i>these </i>are some great friends!

00:20:41.400 --> 00:20:44.240
I'll be back--feed me again, okay?

00:20:44.240 --> 00:20:46.030
You're after her food?

00:20:46.030 --> 00:20:47.030
Uh-huh!

00:20:48.280 --> 00:20:49.290
Hmm?

00:20:50.160 --> 00:20:54.120
Wait--d-did you... just now... "friends"?

00:20:54.120 --> 00:20:55.790
Huh? What?!

00:20:55.790 --> 00:21:00.340
Yep! We're friends,
you and me. So play nice!

00:21:00.340 --> 00:21:04.630
--Oh? Are you perhaps intimidated to
have such a handsome young friend?
--Wh-What is he going on about?

00:21:04.630 --> 00:21:07.300
--Oh? Are you perhaps intimidated to
have such a handsome young friend?
--He <i>must </i>have seen how I was at school.

00:21:07.300 --> 00:21:10.560
--Don't laugh too much, now, Yuzu-<i>chan</i>!
--Everyone hates me! And yet...

00:21:15.100 --> 00:21:18.650
I've never seen that look on
your face, Tamahiko-<i>sama</i>.

00:21:33.080 --> 00:21:34.210
"The Next Day"

00:21:34.210 --> 00:21:36.580
Shima-<i>kun</i>! Begging your pardon!

00:21:37.540 --> 00:21:39.670
He really did come back...

00:21:39.670 --> 00:21:41.460
Welcome!

00:21:41.460 --> 00:21:43.050
What brings you here today?

00:21:45.180 --> 00:21:47.470
And who might that be?

00:21:47.470 --> 00:21:52.180
Oh? Didn't I tell you, Yuzu?
This is my twin sister:

00:21:55.310 --> 00:21:56.940
Kotori Shiratori.

00:22:02.190 --> 00:22:06.110
--What?!
--Oh, my!

00:23:38.620 --> 00:23:42.670
What?! Kotori-<i>chan </i>and
Shiratori-<i>san</i>--twins?

00:23:42.670 --> 00:23:46.960
What a surprise to have Kotori-<i>chan</i>--
my idol--right before my very eyes!

00:23:46.960 --> 00:23:51.930
<i>And </i>she says she wants me
to teach her what love is!
